 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A pronoun replaces a noun so that we do not repeat it.\n• Subject pronouns (before the verb): I, you, he, she, it, we, they — She plays handball.\n• Object pronouns (after a verb or a preposition): me, you, him, her, it, us, them — The coach chose her. Come with us.\n• Possessive pronouns (stand alone): mine, yours, his, hers, ours, theirs — This ball is mine. (Possessive adjectives come before a noun: my ball.)\n• Reflexive pronouns (the same person as the subject): myself, yourself, himself, herself, itself, ourselves, yourselves, themselves — He hurt himself.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Replace the nouns: “Ayuk gave the ball to Ngum and Tabe. The ball belongs to Ayuk.”",
  "steps": [
   "Ayuk → He; the ball → it; Ngum and Tabe → them.",
   "He gave it to them. It is his."
  ],
  "answer": "He gave it to them. It is his.",
  "checks": []
 },
